{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790963986,"nonce":"TjjFNaGMzw5czx/VSio+YahhPgs=","message":"Landed as `1eaa6733` on branch `worktree-agent-a07bf886f0b776fbd`.\n\n`git work sync [REMOTE] [--jira] [--dry-run] [--format json|text]` in `commands/sync.go`,\nregistered in the remote group ahead of `pull` and `push`.\nIt calls `runPull` and `runPush` unchanged — both were already functions of `(env, args)`,\nso the remote resolution (argument, else `git-work.remote`, else `origin`) is theirs —\nand `jiracmd.RunSync(env, dryRun, format)`, a four-line export over `runJiraSync`\nwith no IDs and no `--full`, in between.\n\nBehaviour as decided: a pull that fails stops the command;\na Jira step that fails does not — the push still happens and the error is returned at the end,\nso the command exits 1.\n`--dry-run` is the Jira sync's and is refused without `--jira`,\nin `PreRunE` so nothing is loaded, and again at the top of `runSync`.\n`PreRunE` uses `LoadBackendEnsureUser` only with `--jira`,\nbecause the Jira step writes issues as you while a pull and a push need no identity.\n\nTests in `commands/sync_test.go` over a throwaway local bare remote:\nthe round trip (a second clone's issue comes in, ours goes out),\n`--dry-run` without `--jira` erroring before the pull runs,\nan unbound Jira failing while the push still publishes,\nand two remotes refused.\nA remote with no ref at all cannot be fetched from, so the fixture publishes an identity first.\n\nDocs: the Sync row of the first table in `AGENTS.md`, the push gotcha,\nand a paragraph in JS22 of `doc/design/jira-sync.md`.\n`doc/md` and `doc/man` are stale for `jira` and `view` already, so they were left alone.","files":null}]}